          "filename": "Swale, UC Merced student housing.jpg",
          "caption": "Mimicking nature pays off.  Just like natural site drainage, recessed, planted swales slow, clean, hold and infiltrate precipitation while carrying excess storm water to an on-site retention pond. \n\nThis method replaces the typical catch-basin system of subsurface piping that speeds contaminated water to storm sewers feeding directly into creeks and rivers, and contributing to flash floods and pollution.\nPhotographed at the student housing complex at UC Merced.",
